      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Also sold as Plectranthus scutellarioides; NC State now files it as Coleus. Only one fetched page about this plant (NC State); the Missouri Botanical Garden page failed (certificate error). About a third of the NC State page reached me as a model summary rather than verbatim text, so zones and attribute tags are weaker than the description. Watering: NC State says moist, rich, loose soil and gives no schedule; keep_moist is the agent's mapping. Light: NC State best in part shade, tolerates full shade, may wilt in full sun, needs bright light indoors; stored bright_indirect (agent). Size: NC State mound up to 3 ft both ways. Toxicity: NC State says low-severity poison with diterpenes and skin irritation on contact (allergic rash after repeated contact) but says nothing about pets. The ASPCA coleus page is for a different species (Coleus ampoinicus, Indian borage: toxic to dogs and cats, essential oils, vomiting and diarrhoea), so it is a related-species reading only: pets graded 1 as from_knowledge_verify. Review."
      },
